# Flash layout for the T41NQ, used to assemble the full 16 MiB provisioning
# image. One line per partition:
#
#	<offset>  <size>  <image basename, or "-" to leave erased>
#
# The basename is what the build produces before REPACK_FIRMWARE appends the
# SOC_MODEL suffix; the suffix is added when the image is assembled.
#
# THIS MUST AGREE WITH THE mtdparts LINE IN THE BUILT-IN ENVIRONMENT, which is
# the authority:
#
#	jz_sfc:320k(boot),64k(env),2240k(kernel),8192k(rootfs),5568k(rootfs_data)
#
# in patches-t41/uboot/2026.07/0003-isvp-t41-add-a-built-in-default-environment.patch.
# The assembler checks that the partitions tile the flash exactly - no gap, no
# overlap, and the total is the chip size - so a typo here is caught. It cannot
# know whether the layout matches what the bootloader will tell Linux.
#
# The env partition is deliberately left erased. U-Boot writes its built-in
# default there on first boot (CONFIG_T41_SAVE_DEFAULT_ENV), and that is what
# makes one image safe to flash onto many cameras: each derives its own ethaddr
# from its own eFUSE serial. An environment captured from a working camera would
# clone that camera's MAC onto every unit.
#
# rootfs_data is left erased too, so the overlay starts empty rather than
# carrying whatever the build host happened to leave in it.

0x000000  0x050000  u-boot-with-spl-lzma.bin
0x050000  0x010000  -
0x060000  0x230000  uImage
0x290000  0x800000  rootfs.squashfs
0xa90000  0x570000  -
